  "question": {
    "text": "Number of integral solutions to the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, is equal to _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "105",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>So,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>21</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></math></p><p>So, number of non-negative integral solutions is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mrow><mn>13</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn><none/><mprescripts/><none/><mn>15</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>105</mn></math></p>"
  }
}